Windows LOK: a grabbed window counts as focused

LOK renders off screen. On Linux the headless backend tracks focus
itself, so GrabFocus takes at once. Windows builds have no headless
backend (it needs FreeType and fontconfig), so LOK runs on hidden Win32
windows that never receive the system focus. GrabFocus then waits for a
WM_SETFOCUS that never comes: the document window never has focus, no
paragraph is FOCUSED, and the LOK accessibility listener drops every
caret and selection change. Under LOK on Windows, treat the window as
focused, so the grab switches focus inside the kernel.

--- a/vcl/source/window/mouse.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/window/mouse.cxx
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <config_feature_desktop.h>
 #include <config_vclplug.h>
 
+#include <comphelper/lok.hxx>
 #include <tools/time.hxx>
 
 #include <LibreOfficeKit/LibreOfficeKitEnums.h>
@@ -189,6 +190,12 @@ static bool IsWindowFocused(const WindowImpl& rWinImpl)
     if (rWinImpl.mbFakeFocusSet)
         return true;
 
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    // LOK's hidden Win32 windows never get the system focus.
+    if (comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::isActive())
+        return true;
+#endif
+
     return false;
 }
 
